        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "864a7273-5f39-58c0-9403-9214e53b490d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marley Shelton, David M. Evans, Ronny Yu, Angus Macfadyen, Mario Yedidia, Kevin Smith\n- Films: Grand Canyon, The Sandlot, Pleasantville, Never Been Kissed, Sugar & Spice, Valentine, Warriors of Virtue, Warriors of Virtue: The Return to Tao\n- Topics: film debuts, teen-oriented films, coming-of-age baseball films, martial arts fantasy films, actor deaths\n\nFacts:\n- Marley Shelton made her film debut in \"Grand Canyon\" in 1991.\n- \"The Sandlot\" is a 1993 American coming-of-age baseball film co-written and directed by David M. Evans about a group of young baseball players during the summer of 1962.\n- Marley Shelton appeared in teen-audience films including \"The Sandlot\" in 1993, \"Pleasantville\" in 1998, and \"Never Been Kissed\" in 1999.\n- \"Warriors of Virtue\" is a 1997 Chinese-American martial arts fantasy film directed by Ronny Yu and starring Angus Macfadyen, Mario Yedidia, and Marley Shelton.\n- Marley Shelton also appeared in the teen-audience films \"Sugar & Spice\" and \"Valentine\" in 2001.\n- Kevin Smith died in February 2002 after falling from a prop tower.\n- \"Warriors of Virtue: The Return to Tao\" was the last film to star Kevin Smith.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4c784e75-474b-55e5-b989-7c5aa2351d66",
        "text": "Page: Marley Shelton. Sentence: She made her film debut in \"Grand Canyon\" (1991), and followed with a line of roles in films aimed at teenage audiences, including \"The Sandlot\" (1993), \"Pleasantville\" (1998), \"Never Been Kissed\" (1999), \"Sugar & Spice\" (2001) and \" Valentine\" (2001).\nPage: The Sandlot. Sentence: The Sandlot is a 1993 American coming-of-age baseball film co-written and directed by David M. Evans, which tells the story of a group of young baseball players during the summer of 1962.\nPage: Warriors of Virtue. Sentence: Warriors of Virtue is a 1997 Chinese-American martial arts fantasy film directed by Ronny Yu and starring Angus Macfadyen, Mario Yedidia, and Marley Shelton.\nPage: Warriors of Virtue: The Return to Tao. Sentence: This is the last film to star actor Kevin Smith, who died in February 2002 after falling from a prop tower.",
